# K11 - The human + agent team. Kata sandbox sketch (plan section 3.6).
# [K11-nn] sketch IDs are recognised by validate_architecture / trace and ignored by the
# CI adl-coverage gate. Never [TR-*]; promotion is decided only at K12 (architecture/REVIEW.md).
DESCRIPTION K11 - the written instructions, the owner register and the commit history are the team's governance
CATEGORY Governance
NAMESPACE TrK11NS
DEFINE SYSTEM Total Recall K11 Sandbox AS trk11
    DEFINE COMPONENT Instructions AS instructions
    DEFINE COMPONENT Owner Register AS register
    DEFINE COMPONENT Commit History AS history

# Course pp. 47-50, 69-74: a team of humans and agents works from what is written down. CLAUDE.md,
# GOVERNANCE.md, REVIEW.md and ARCHITECTURE.md are read before every change. A removed test file or a
# retired TR-* ID sends a contributor to a rule that is gone. A line that says "pending" may name one
# that does not exist yet.
ASSERT(Instructions: every test file and every TR-* ID named in CLAUDE.md, GOVERNANCE.md, REVIEW.md and ARCHITECTURE.md exists, unless the line says it is pending) # [K11-01]

# GOVERNANCE.md section 1 gives each ADL file an owner, a trigger and a remediation. A new ADL file with
# no row is a rule with no owner.
ASSERT(Owner Register: every production ADL file has a row in the governance register, and every row names a file that exists) # [K11-02]

# Commit history is the audit trail of the team, human and agent alike: a commit that changes an ADL
# file carries a test, or a governance, review or backlog record. Checked on the real history only when
# the clone is not shallow.
ASSERT(Commit History: every commit that changes an ADL file also changes a test or a governance, review or backlog record) # [K11-03]

# Not re-asserted, answered with existing evidence (answers.md): agents are contributors, never
# approvers (GOVERNANCE section 2, TR-Q2, TR-Q4, TR-Q5), dispositions for a failed assertion (GOVERNANCE
# section 3). Checks that cannot be deterministic stay interactive reviews (checklist section 9).
